# The fixes to the hooks part of step 28's fixes, from the pre-push
# review of their third pull request: a trust store that cannot be read
# holds a project's hooks back, their gates failing, and takes nothing
# away; a hook's replacement reaches the model with no selector; a name
# the managed file locks, or one of the user's hooks takes, holds
# nothing; a project's run going on stops when its trust is taken away;
# and an observer is not handed a file that waits for the yes.

[break] unreadable-store-withdraws
rule: A trust store a reload cannot read takes nothing away from the session: the project's hooks are held back, not withdrawn.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/reload.rs
in: withdraw_untrusted
find: if store_unread {
replace: if false && store_unread {
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_trust::sys_an_unreadable_trust_store_holds_a_projects_gates_until_it_is_read

[break] unread-project-gate-lapses
rule: While the trust store cannot be read, a project's approved gate fails, refusing what it gates.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hook_points.rs
in: on_now
find: hook.while_unread.as_ref()
replace: None::<&Arc<dyn Hook>>
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_trust::sys_an_unreadable_trust_store_holds_a_projects_gates_until_it_is_read

[break] store-read-again-keeps-hooks-back
rule: Once a look reads the trust store again and it trusts the project, the project's hooks are as they were.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/reload.rs
in: withdraw_untrusted
find: } else if runs_projects && let Some(note) = hooks.project_store_unread(false) {
replace: } else if false && let Some(note) = hooks.project_store_unread(false) {
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_trust::sys_an_unreadable_trust_store_holds_a_projects_gates_until_it_is_read

[break] in-force-ignores-the-projects-trust
rule: A project's hook commands are the session's only while its trust is as the session opened with.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hook_command.rs
in: HookCommands::in_force
find: source == Source::User || self.project() == ProjectHooks::InForce
replace: source == Source::User || self.project() != ProjectHooks::Withdrawn || true
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_trust::sys_a_projects_hook_command_stops_with_its_trust

[break] running-project-run-not-stopped
rule: Each run of a project's hook still going when its trust is taken away is stopped, its process with it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hook_command.rs
in: HookCommands::run_cancel
find: Source::Project => self.project.child()
replace: Source::Project => CancelToken::new()
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_trust::sys_a_projects_hook_run_going_on_stops_when_its_trust_is_taken_away

[break] observer-handed-a-secret-file
rule: An observer of tool.before whose {path} would take a file that waits for the person's yes does not run for the call.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hook_command.rs
in: HookCommands::run
find: && hook.uses_path()
replace: && hook.uses_path() && !hook.observe
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it hook_trust::sys_a_users_hook_is_handed_a_secret_file_only_after_the_yes

[break] replaced-note-keeps-selectors
rule: The note that tells the model a hook replaced its arguments carries no variation selector.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/hooks.rs
in: replaced_note
find: cineris_base::visible_to_the_model(&replaced.arguments.to_string())
replace: cineris_base::visible(&replaced.arguments.to_string())
packages: cineris-agent
caught-by:
    cineris-agent hooks::tests::a_replacements_note_carries_no_selector_to_the_model

[break] locked-project-hook-holds-gates
rule: An approved project hook whose name the managed file locks holds nothing: the administrator's word, not a removal.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hooks.rs
in: Configured::of
find: .extend(loaded.project_hooks_locked.iter().cloned());
replace: .extend(Vec::<String>::new());
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core ext::hooks::tests::an_approved_projects_hook_holds_both_gates_once_not_as_approved

[break] taken-project-hook-holds-gates
rule: An approved project hook whose name one of the user's own hooks takes holds nothing, whether or not the project's file turns it off.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/hooks.rs
in: Configured::of
find: configured.project_yielded.push(hook.name.clone());
replace: let _ = &hook.name;
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core ext::hooks::tests::an_approved_projects_hook_holds_both_gates_once_not_as_approved
